{"content":[{"c":["BAMAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Hebrew word meaning height, ridge, or elevation in the topography of the land (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.1.19,25","r":"2Sam.1.19,25","rawR":"2Sam.1.19,25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.1.19,25","value":"2Sam.1.19,25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 1:19, 25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.22.34","r":"2Sam.22.34","rawR":"2Sam.22.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.22.34","value":"2Sam.22.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:34"},"); transliterated into English once (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.20.29","r":"Ezek.20.29","rawR":"Ezek.20.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.20.29","value":"Ezek.20.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 20:29"},"; see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). It is a term designating hills or mountains overlooking the Arnon River (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.28","r":"Num.21.28","rawR":"Num.21.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.28","value":"Num.21.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:28"},"). The plural form (Bamoth) alone or as the first part of a compound is used for the name of towns in Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.19-20","r":"Num.21.19-20","rawR":"Num.21.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.19-20","value":"Num.21.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:19-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.22.41","r":"Num.22.41","rawR":"Num.22.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.22.41","value":"Num.22.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:41"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.17","r":"Josh.13.17","rawR":"Josh.13.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.17","value":"Josh.13.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Metaphorically, the word connotes a place of security (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.32.13","r":"Deut.32.13","rawR":"Deut.32.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.32.13","value":"Deut.32.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 32:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Hab.3.19","r":"Hab.3.19","rawR":"Hab.3.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hab.3.19","value":"Hab.3.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hb 3:19"},"), as well as the high ground that a military commander wished to control in battle. Possession of an enemy’s “heights” was synonymous with subjection of that enemy (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.29","r":"Deut.33.29","rawR":"Deut.33.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.29","value":"Deut.33.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 33:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.36.2","r":"Ezek.36.2","rawR":"Ezek.36.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.36.2","value":"Ezek.36.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 36:2"},"). The word seems to combine both literal and figurative connotations in several references to Jerusalem, a “high place” in ruin overgrown with scrub vegetation (",{"href":"?bref=Mic.3.12","r":"Mic.3.12","rawR":"Mic.3.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.3.12","value":"Mic.3.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 3:12"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.26.18","r":"Jer.26.18","rawR":"Jer.26.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.26.18","value":"Jer.26.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 26:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.36.1-2","r":"Ezek.36.1-2","rawR":"Ezek.36.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.36.1-2","value":"Ezek.36.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 36:1-2"},"). “High place” was also a special, or technical, term in Canaanite religion, designating a local shrine on a hill near a town or village, in contrast to the large temples located throughout the land."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=HighPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"HighPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"HighPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"High Place"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bamah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 1:19, 25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.1.19,25","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.1.19,25","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.1.19,25"},{"anchorText":"22:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.22.34","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.22.34","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.22.34"},{"anchorText":"Ez 20:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.20.29","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.20.29","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.20.29"},{"anchorText":"Nm 21:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.28","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.28","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.28"},{"anchorText":"Nm 21:19-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.19-20","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.19-20","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.19-20"},{"anchorText":"22:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.22.41","rawQueryValue":"Num.22.41","sourceRefExact":"Num.22.41"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.17","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.17","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.17"},{"anchorText":"Dt 32:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.32.13","rawQueryValue":"Deut.32.13","sourceRefExact":"Deut.32.13"},{"anchorText":"Hb 3:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hab.3.19","rawQueryValue":"Hab.3.19","sourceRefExact":"Hab.3.19"},{"anchorText":"Dt 33:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.29","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.29","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.29"},{"anchorText":"Ez 36:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.36.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.36.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.36.2"},{"anchorText":"Mi 3:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.3.12","rawQueryValue":"Mic.3.12","sourceRefExact":"Mic.3.12"},{"anchorText":"Jer 26:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.26.18","rawQueryValue":"Jer.26.18","sourceRefExact":"Jer.26.18"},{"anchorText":"Ez 36:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.36.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.36.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.36.1-2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ba552229bc170673fc08f1775fe5ae28d44add49a910b0b3d52a15a3a9439796","sourceItemName":"Bamah","sourceItemOrder":60,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bamah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bamah","title":"Bamah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}